triage:c6_qa1_RBP_F001 a triage:Finding ;
 triage:id "RBP-F001" ;
 triage:severity "minor" ;
 triage:reviewer "rust-best-practices-agent" ;
 triage:status "open" ;
 triage:reviewed_commit "b72712ff3a060e97a8229e48f0b29c6536020e54" ;
 triage:file "crates/sc-cron-commands/src/executor/errors.rs" ;
 triage:issue "All invalid expressions and invalid schedule specifications lose their safe failure category at the command boundary. The response only says 'invalid cron request' and asks callers to correct unspecified fields/limits, so callers cannot distinguish an invalid cron expression from timeout, name, payload, or environment validation failures." ;
 triage:action "Keep CRON.INVALID_INPUT and value-free messages, but attach a bounded static reason or field identifier and specific recovery guidance where the adapter knows the cause. At minimum distinguish BadExpression from InvalidSpec; local generation, cursor, limit, and aggregate-size checks can identify their own static reason without forwarding request values or provider prose." ;
 triage:verification_source "https://github.com/randlee/sc-runtime/pull/121#issuecomment-6676426858" .

triage:c6_qa1_FTQ_001 a triage:Finding ;
 triage:id "FTQ-001" ;
 triage:severity "critical" ;
 triage:reviewer "flaky-test-qa" ;
 triage:status "open" ;
 triage:reviewed_commit "b72712ff3a060e97a8229e48f0b29c6536020e54" ;
 triage:file "template/crates/daemon/src/observability_adapter_tests.rs" ;
 triage:issue "The subprocess watchdog does not bound physical cleanup. Drop ignores the kill result and calls Child::wait without a deadline; the timeout branch also calls unbounded wait after kill. On a failed termination or stalled physical exit, the supposedly bounded fixture can hang indefinitely, including while unwinding an earlier status-inspection error." ;
 triage:action "Consume the C2 bounded physical-reap correction: retain the owned child through bounded termination and observed physical completion on timeout, status failure and Drop paths, with explicit failure diagnostics. Preserve existing budgets and add causal cleanup failure witnesses; do not retry, pad, serialize, skip or kill-and-forget." ;
 triage:verification_source "https://github.com/randlee/sc-runtime/pull/121#issuecomment-6676426858" .

triage:c6_qa1_FTQ_002 a triage:Finding ;
 triage:id "FTQ-002" ;
 triage:severity "important" ;
 triage:reviewer "flaky-test-qa" ;
 triage:status "open" ;
 triage:reviewed_commit "b72712ff3a060e97a8229e48f0b29c6536020e54" ;
 triage:file "crates/sc-cron/tests/hook_environment/owned_child_unix_tests.rs" ;
 triage:issue "The supposedly pinned launcher exits naturally after time.sleep(30). If the parent is descheduled after the ready marker long enough for that exit, the original early-return-on-inspection-error bug can satisfy reaped_at_return and falsely pass. The related inspector expiry witness at line130 can instead fail spuriously: bounded_wait_with checks try_wait before the forced expiry callback, so an already naturally exited child returns success rather than the expected expiry error." ;
 triage:action "Hold each ready child until explicit owner termination or owner release, using a causal readiness/lifetime handshake. Keep a bounded owning Session on every path, including assertion failure, and retain a negative implementation check that fails at the return-boundary assertion. Do not extend the 30-second sleep, retry or serialize." ;
 triage:verification_source "https://github.com/randlee/sc-runtime/pull/121#issuecomment-6676426858" .
